1.3.0-dev (not yet released)

- TODO: New: Introduced "Cast" feature to quickly cast an online video to any DLNA (UPnP) renderer found on the network
- TODO: New: Allow resolving proxy modes and scheduled proactive resolving for Custom Playlists, enabling for locally-curated, multi-service "Watch Later" playlists
- TODO: New: Quick "Add to playlist" UI for Custom Playlists being used as local Watch Later lists (also allowing reordering and deleting items)
- New: Introduced an "auto" service, allowing yt-dlp to chose the extractor automatically, which is the new default (please update yt-dlna.conf accordingly if upgrading)
- Improved: Faster startup of ffmpeg remux process
- Improved: New default DASH format selector for YouTube, fixing URLs not being resolved on multi-language videos (please copy from yt-dlna.conf.example if upgrading)

1.2.0 (2026-08-30)

- New: Custom sync intervals per playlist
- New: Time of last playlist sync is shown in Web UI now
- New: Command-line options and Web UI buttons to rebuild playlist library and purge CDN URL cache
- New: Command-line options --sync and --serve can be used together, forcing an initial sync of all playlists before launching the daemon
- New: Logs are visible in the Web UI with live update
- New: Added proxy routes for explicitly selecting remux target formats (/remux/mp4, /remux/ts)
- Improved: Logging now uses colors and has configurable verbosity (via configuration and command-line option)
- Improved: Optimized handling (caching) of the configuration file for minimized disk I/O
- Improved: Saving JSON files is done via a save-replace operation, avoiding conflicts with external processes writing to them
- Improved: Clearer wording in Web UI regarding settings inheritance for playlists
- Improved: Some more Web UI tweaks, like improved mobile views etc.
- Fixed: Wrong CDN URLs could get stored in cache if resolution previously had failed for one or more videos
- Fixed: Stale ffmpeg processes could remain in memory after client disconnects in TS mode

1.1.0 (2026-08-16)

- New: Introduced on-the-fly DASH remultiplexing via ffmpeg
- New: Added Web UI (dashboard and configuration interface) with light and dark mode
- New: Added Custom Playlists feature for hierarchical, locally-curated playlists
- New: Added more proxy routes to select specific modes independently from the default operating mode
- Improved: Optimized URL resolving performance by letting yt-dlp batch-resolve a collection of playlist items at once
- Improved: Optimized DLNA Server compatibility with more clients
- Improved: Configuration file is automatically created from example on first run
- Fixed: Fixed a possible race condition when updating URL cache file
- Fixed: Config file was not correctly interpreted as UTF-8 if running on Windows

1.0.0 (2026-08-03)

- Initial release to the public
